Chapter: BrowserOfflineLoadTest
  cites Browser chapter PageRuntime
  cites Browser chapter PageSandbox
  cites Browser chapter TrustManager
  cites Browser chapter ContentCache
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `resolve-and-load` is the browser's default load path and is local-only, so
 that the app carries no Network effect and `GopDesk`, which embeds it as a
 pane, does not have to declare one up its whole chain to `opening`.

 This pins both halves. A `codex://local` address still loads, so the
 narrowing did not break the pages that work; a named host answers
 PageFetchError rather than reaching for a socket.

 The stronger guard is the one that cannot be read from the output: this
 chapter's `opening` declares `[Console]` alone. If the `NamedAddress` arm
 is ever wired back to `load-remote-page`, `resolve-and-load` regains
 `Network.Read, Network.Write`, and THIS FILE STOPS COMPILING with CDX2031
 rather than quietly passing. The recorded numbers are the weaker half.

Section: Test

  res-code : PageLoadResult -> Integer
  res-code (r) =
    when r
      is PageLoaded (tree) (title) (caps) -> 1
      is PageCompileError (m) -> 2
      is PageFetchError (m) -> 3
      is PageTrustDenied (t) -> 4
      is PageSizeDenied (s) -> 5

  res-title : PageLoadResult -> Text
  res-title (r) =
    when r
      is PageLoaded (tree) (title) (caps) -> title
      is PageCompileError (m) -> m
      is PageFetchError (m) -> m
      is PageTrustDenied (t) -> "trust"
      is PageSizeDenied (s) -> "size"

  probe : Text -> PageLoadResult
  probe (addr) =
    resolve-and-load addr sandbox-default-config (trust-store-new []) (cache-new 64) 800 600

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (res-code (probe "codex://local/newtab")))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (res-code (probe "codex://local/hello")))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (res-code (probe "codex://example.com/page")))
    print-line-uni (res-title (probe "codex://example.com/page"))
  end
